{
  "summary": "P1 \u2013 office-wide internet outage. Reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3): \"The whole office just lost internet. Nobody on the floor can work.\" Which office/floor wasn't stated; the user's timezone is America/New_York. Checks: account active, no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online with last check-in 2026-10-09 14:58 UTC and no warnings. That check-in may have happened before the outage, or the laptop may be on another connection such as a hotspot, so it doesn't rule out an outage. KB-014 says to escalate when the office network is down for several people. Tier 1 tools can't check the office network (WAN/ISP circuit, firewall, core switches, DHCP/DNS). Needed: check the site edge/ISP link right away, find out how many users are affected, and send updates to the floor. Contact Priya for site details.",
  "reason": "P1 office-wide outage; KB-014 escalation criteria met; network infrastructure beyond Tier 1 tools"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for reporting this. Because the whole office is affected, we've marked it top priority and sent it straight to our Tier 2 network engineers, who will look at the office's internet connection and network equipment. They may contact you to confirm which office and floor are down and roughly how many people are affected. If you have that information, please reply with it. That will help them work faster. Until then, anyone with urgent work can use a phone hotspot to get online. We'll keep you posted.",
  "internal_note": "P1: office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3). Her account is active with no problems. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online (last check-in 14:58 UTC, no warnings). That check-in may be from before the outage, or the laptop may be on another connection, so it doesn't rule out a site outage. KB-014's escalation rule applies (office network down for several people), and the ticket is P1. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) to check the site's internet link, firewall and switches. Which site is affected still needs to be confirmed. No fix actions were queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
